.TH 9SHARE-INIT 8 "2026" "9share" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
9share-init \- make the 9share daemon start at boot the way this machine starts services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 9share\-init detect
.br
.B 9share\-init enable
.RB [ \-\-from\-package ]
.br
.B 9share\-init disable
.RB [ \-\-from\-package ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 9share\-init
finds out which init system runs this machine and does what that one needs to start the root daemon of
.BR 9share (8)
at boot and now.  The package runs it when it is installed and removed; it is installed in the libexec directory of 9share
(for the package,
.IR /usr/libexec/9share ),
not in the path, and may be run again by root.  It never fails: what it cannot do it says, with what to type instead.
.TP
.B detect
Print one of
.BR systemd ,
.BR wsl2 ,
.BR wsl1 ,
.BR openrc ,
.BR runit ,
.B sysv
or
.BR none .
systemd is checked first (it includes WSL2 with systemd=true in
.IR /etc/wsl.conf );
then WSL2 and WSL1, told apart by
.IR /proc/version ;
then OpenRC, runit, sysvinit.
.TP
.B enable
.RS
.TP
.B systemd
.B "systemctl enable \-\-now 9share.service"
.TP
.B wsl2
.B "9share wsl\-boot"
(the [boot] command of
.IR /etc/wsl.conf ),
then the daemon is started at once.
.TP
.B openrc
.B "rc\-update add 9share default"
and start it, if
.I /etc/init.d/9share
is there.
.TP
.B sysv
.B "update\-rc.d 9share defaults"
and start it.
.TP
.B wsl1, runit, none
Nothing is set up; the message says why, or how to run
.BR "sudo 9share boot \-\-detach" .
WSL1 has no 9p support in its kernel, so 9share cannot mount there.
.RE
.TP
.B disable
Undo it for wsl2 (the boot command is removed, and a command of the user's that was kept comes back) and openrc.  For systemd and
sysvinit the package's own scripts stop and disable the service.
.PP
.B \-\-from\-package
says that the maintainer script of the Debian package calls it after debhelper has already enabled and started the service under
systemd and sysvinit: for those two only the message is printed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NINESHARE_ROOT
A prefix put before every path that is looked at (/proc/version, /run, /etc, /sbin).  For tests, which pretend to be each kind of machine.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 9share (8)
